isaspec: params on derived bitset fields; a field an override defines wins

Two changes the SGX545 ISA description (src/sgx/isa/sgx.xml) needs:

- A <derived> field may have a bitset type, so an operand whose number,
  bank and extension bits are scattered across the instruction can be
  rebuilt by an expression and decoded by one operand hierarchy. Such a
  field needs <param>s like a plain bitset field: parse them, and give the
  encoder's bitset_params struct their names.

- When two or more <override>s of a bitset define the same field, the
  encoder emitted, inside an override's branch, the other overrides'
  definitions as an if/else ladder whose last "else" (the default case,
  already seen) was dropped, so the dangling "else" captured the next
  field's encoding. The definition in the case being encoded wins: stop
  looking once it is found.

diff --git a/src/compiler/isaspec/encode.py b/src/compiler/isaspec/encode.py
